// apps/server/package.json: the Fastify backend.
//
// ⚠️  Delete all comments when done (JSON doesn't allow comments).
//
// Fields to write:
//
//   "name"          e.g. "@jejune/server" (same scope as shared)
//   "version"       "0.0.0"
//   "private": true
//   "type": "module"   Native ESM in Node.
//
//   "scripts"
//     "dev"        tsx in watch mode on your entry file (e.g. src/main.ts).
//                  tsx runs TypeScript directly in Node and restarts on change.
//                  It also compiles @jejune/shared's .ts source.
//     "typecheck"  tsc with the no-emit flag
//     "start"      plain tsx on the entry file is fine for a localhost-only
//                  app. You can add a real bundled build step later if you
//                  need one (PLAN §15 "decisions to postpone").
//
//   "dependencies"
//     The link to shared. Add it with the CLI so the protocol is right:
//       pnpm --filter @jejune/server add @jejune/shared@workspace:*
//     This writes  "@jejune/shared": "workspace:*". The `workspace:`
//     protocol means "always use the local package, never the registry", and
//     pnpm symlinks node_modules/@jejune/shared → packages/shared.
//
//   "devDependencies"
//     tsx and @types/node:
//       pnpm --filter @jejune/server add -D tsx @types/node
//     (typescript is installed at the root, so you don't need it here.)
//
// Later in Milestone 0 (not part of the workspace scaffold): fastify, zod,
// drizzle-orm + better-sqlite3 (+ drizzle-kit as a dev dep), pino.
